  "key_findings": [
    "Combo candidate improves all three same-window comparisons: 1626 CAGR +0.40pp, 1217 +0.25pp, 1226 +0.06pp.",
    "Sharpe improves in all three windows: 1626 +0.030, 1217 +0.013, 1226 +0.009.",
    "MaxDD improves slightly in all windows; full-cycle MaxDD improvement is +0.08pp.",
    "ETF NAV is identical between B0 and candidate in every window, so differences come from the stock sleeve only.",
    "Full-cycle D5 exits count is 27; improvement is real but modest, so it is not enough for baseline promotion by itself.",
    "Trade-level D5 audit: 15/27 exits are effective drawdown prevention, 5/27 are churn/sold-too-early, 3/27 are mixed, 4/27 are small neutral.",
    "By sell amount, effective exits are 58.0% of D5 sell value; churn exits are 18.7%; mixed exits are 23.1%.",
    "The cleanest next step is to audit whether mixed/churn cases share a narrower eligibility pattern before changing the rule.",
    "Watch combo AB completed for 1626, 1217, and 1226 with 12 unified-runtime combo runs.",
    "Watch-day10 is best on full-cycle 1226: CAGR +0.44pp, Sharpe +0.0206, MaxDD +0.06pp, Calmar +0.0132 versus same-window B0.",
    "Watch-day10 does not repair recent 2025-2026 drag: combo -2.88pp and stock leg -9.13pp versus B0 over 2025-2026.",
    "Watch-day5 is unstable: it slightly wins 1626 CAGR but loses 1217 and 1226 CAGR.",
    "Decision: do not promote V4; hold watch-day10 as research-only and next study should isolate deep early MAE behavior."
  ],
